# Line endings are a property of this repository, not of whoever clones it.
#
# This machine happens to set `core.autocrlf=input` globally, which
# normalises on commit — but that is machine-local configuration that does
# not travel to a CI runner or to anyone else's clone. Declaring it here
# makes it the repository's own rule.
#
# It matters because these images ship shell entrypoints: a CRLF on a
# shebang line makes the interpreter unfindable at runtime, and the error
# names neither the file nor the cause.
#
# `mixed-line-ending` in .pre-commit-config.yaml is the complement, not a
# substitute: it catches a file carrying more than one ending style, which
# is what a half-converted file looks like.
* text=auto eol=lf
